risk7day":"Medium","idp_source":"gtwo_kml_202610192351","idp_filedate":1792453916000,"nhcTitle":"Off the East Coast of the United States (AL93)","discussion":"A storm-force non-tropical low pressure area is currently attached  to an occluded frontal boundary a few hundred miles off the  southeast coast of the United States. This low is likely to move  slowly north-northeastward over the next couple of days. If the low  remains over the Gulf Stream, it could develop organized shower and  thunderstorm activity. If the low is also then able to separate  from frontal features, it could briefly acquire subtropical cyclone  characteristics during the middle to latter portion of this week.  The system is expected to move northeastward away from the the  eastern United States later this week, and environmental conditions  are expected to become unfavorable for subtropical or tropical  development by the weekend.  1. Regardless of the status of the system, high winds, coastal  flooding, and dangerous surf are expected along portions of the U.S.  East Coast during the next few days. For more information, please  consult statements and warnings from local National Weather Service  offices and the Weather Prediction Center, along with High Seas  Forecasts and Storm Warnings issued by the National Weather Service. \n Formation chance through 48 hours...low...20 percent. \n Formation chance through 7 days...medium...40 percent.","disturbance":1}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-94.1451540775395,8.980150604526402],[-94.08327868239941,9.017201169372585],[-94.02156566098897,9.054965126325149],[-93.96020173189656,9.093450579151465],[-93.89937361371061,9.13266563161891],[-93.8392680250195,9.172618387494854],[-93.78007168441167,9.213316950546673],[-93.72197131047547,9.25476942454174],[-93.66515362179932,9.296983913247429],[-93.60980533697163,9.339968520431112],[-93.5561131745808,9.383731349860165],[-93.50426385321522,9.42828050530196],[-93.4544440914633